<section class="mn-s mn-dr" id="drift"><div class="mn-dr-i pxw"><img data-px=".12" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564091880021-bb02f2b2928d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&h=1000&q=75" alt="a clock face with a red seconds hand" width="1800" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mn-w mn-dr-g"><div><p class="mn-ey">Drift calculator</p><h2 class="rv">How far will it wander?</h2><p class="mn-p">Watches gain or lose a little each day. Set your watch&rsquo;s daily rate to see where it will be in a week, a month and a year.</p><label class="mn-lab" for="dr-s">Seconds per day <output id="dr-o">+5 s</output><input type="range" id="dr-s" min="-30" max="30" value="5"></label><div class="mn-chips" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Movement type"><label><input type="radio" name="mv" value="m" checked><span>Mechanical</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="mv" value="q"><span>Quartz</span></label></div></div><div class="mn-dr-o" id="dr-r" aria-live="polite"></div></div></section>

<section class="mn-qt"><div class="mn-w mn-qt-g"><div class="mn-qt-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512856246663-647a81ef198e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=760&q=75" alt="a black and white close-up of clock hands" width="760" height="760" loading="lazy"></div><blockquote><p class="rv">A minute is long enough to be late, and short enough to forget. Watches remember it for us.</p><cite>The Minute editors</cite></blockquote></div></section>

